Z||000002||Shaun41178||04-18-2000||10:32 PM||||Eric, glad you saw this as I couldn't find your email addy.<P>TNT on Fri is from 6pm-11pm.  They also allow you to stay over in the track for free for those people that have a long way to drive and don't want to leave that night.  <P>i work till 6 on Fri.  However I am going to see if i can switch with a fellow coworker so I can get off at 4 instead of 6.  that will give me an hour to get ready and an hour to get there.  I am going to guess if the weather is good that there will be quite a few cars there but with 5 hours to run 5-6 runs are possible so no need to worry about not getting to run.  If the turnout is rather small you can expect around 10 runs or so.  <P>I will keep you updated whether or not I will be able to switch with my coworker.  If not then I probably won't go and will wait for another time as I won't get to Norwalk till around 8 or so.<P>Anyone else interested in going??<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||04-20-2000||08:56 AM||||Any news?||||reg||5
Z||000004||Shaun41178||04-20-2000||05:58 PM||||Well eric the news is rain.  Watching the forecast for tomorrow and they say rain all day.  So I didn't even ask my coworker if he wanted to switch or not.  There will be other days to go.   <P>In fact with all the rain we have had here in Toledo my street was flooded all day.  I was able to get off the street at 4 to go to work to tell my boss and he gave me a load of crap like I was a liar or something and that my street wasn't flooded all day.  But it was flooded all day.  Last time I tried to drive through water as high as it was today I burned up my starter as water got into it.  Not again.  Not worth it.  Perhaps this Wed or even this upcoming fri we could go weather pending again of course.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||04-20-2000||10:54 PM||||Good call.  Rain wouldn't be something I'd want to deal with.<P>Guess you guys up North got more rain then us.  I've driven my Fiero on some very wet roads before.  One time I was driving with my friend after a big downpour to some Chinese buffet.  I wasn't that familiar with the area, so when I saw the building I turned.  Unfortunatly, I couldn't see the curb and missed the driveway completly.  I drove down into a ditch about 3 feet deep with a storm sewer grate at the bottom.  I think that's what saved me cause I was able to get traction and wheel my way out.  No damage to the Fiero though, but I just about $hit my pants when I saw how deep the ditch really was after the water had drained away.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||04-27-2000||06:58 PM||||Eric Good news for tomorrow.  As I write this the weather forecast for tomorrow is supposed to be sunny and around 60.  I plan on going to norwalk tomorrow after I get off of work.  i work till 6 but plan on going straight from work to Norwalk.  If I leave exactly at 6 I will get there around 7:15 or so.  I probably won't get out of there till more like 6:30 though so I probably w0n't be there till almost 8.  not bad and it will give me 3 hours to run it.<P>Hope to see you there.  Cost is $10<P>If you go look for a red 85 GT.  I will probably be the only Fiero there so that will make it easy.  If I see a 88 Fastback I will guess that is you.<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eric||04-27-2000||11:07 PM||||I can't go.  I have to stay and feed my mom's horses for the entire weekend.  I'd much prefer to leave them hungry for a night but I don't think dead horses are much use for someone who want's to ride them.  Good news is the first autoX of the year is on Sunday, and since it's in town, I can feed the horses, go race, and come back and feed the horses again.  I thought about going up to the local 1/8 mile track for some test/tune tommorow so I can get the thing ready for the trek up North.  Sorry I can't make it.  We should get in touch so we can coordinate our schedules and prey the weather will cooperate.<P>Hey, I need the real deal on the N2O so you can definatly count on me coming up there sometime and bother you with a never ending session of nitrous questions.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||05-03-2000||02:30 PM||||Shaun, did you ever get to go?  If you're planning on going this week or next, please tell me.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shaun41178||05-03-2000||07:53 PM||||Yea I did end up going last fri. Might have been good that you didn't go.  Lots of cars and I mean lots.  Plus the lights didn't come on when it got dark so there was a like a 2 hour delay.  I didn't leave there till 12:00 and didn't get home till 1 or so.<P>i didn't run too well either.  Reason is my nitrous filter was glogged so no nitrous gas could get through.  Well some could get through cause of the extreme preasure but only the equivalant of a 30 shot.  I ran a 15.2 both runs on my nitrous.  Not very fast at all but with the filter clogged what can you expect right?  So I have the filter cleaned now but the thing is crossthreaded/stripped and so is my nitrous solenoid.  SO now I need a new nitrous filter and a solenoid so if I go this fri I wont' be running the nitrous unless I can come up with something by then to keep it from leaking.  DOn't have the money to spend right now for a new solenoid either right now.  Perhaps I can put a load of teflon goo on it to keep it from leaking.<P>If weather is good this fri then I will go.  I won't be there till around 7:30 however as I work till 6.<P>Funny thign about fri night thoguh is that I raced a turbo supra like an 89 model.  Guy said he had $40k in his car in mods.  He should have creamed me.  I beat him as he ran a 15.6 to my 15.2.  It was kind of funny.  I should have whipped him more if my nitrous was working properly.  I also beat a 99 Stang V6 that had 215 dyno hp at the crank.  He tore the engine out and had it dynoed at his dads shop so he said.  I beat him too.  He ran a 16 flat to my 15.2 again.<P>So if weather is good then I will hope to see you there.  Just email me or post here if things change.<P>Shaun<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||05-03-2000||10:51 PM||||Sounds like a good plan.  I'll post back on this thread tommorow night to confirm.  I heard on the news today that the weather is supposed to be super nice and warm.  Also, if you're not able to go, post on this thread.  I'll take a look just before I leave which should be around 4:30 or so.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Eric||05-04-2000||02:20 PM||||Do I need a helmet?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Shaun41178||05-04-2000||09:41 PM||||No you don't need a helmet.<P>make sure all the lug nuts are on the wheels.  They won't check these but even so I wouldn't want a wheel flying off at 80 mph.  Make sure windshield is not cracked.  They probably wont' let you run if it is.  If you have a sunroof make sure that is on.  I will walk you through your first couple of times if you want me to.  When you run the windows must be up.  Will allow the car to run faster though as less wind resistance.  When you get there inflate your front tires to like 40 psi.  I can show you where to do that if you can't find it.  Might want to drop a few psi in the rear tires to help with traction.   <P>If you really want to run some fast times bring a bag or two of ice with you.  They have Ice there as well but I have no idea what it costs.  I would think around $2 a bag when you can get it from a convenience store for like $1 a bag.  That should take like a .2 off your. et from the cooler intake temps.<P>Still on for me.  i got my flat taken care of.  A different set of rims on it the 15's actually.  So look for a red 85 Gt with the stock 14 inch rims on it and also the grey 15 inch diamond spoke wheels.  That will be me.<P>See you there.  YEA BABY!<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000013||Eric||05-04-2000||11:42 PM||||Hi-Ho Hi-Ho  It's off to Norwalk I go...<P>The part about the 15" rims really confused me, but I think I'll be able to spot your car easily enough.  I'm in a black GT with gold rims, if you didn't know already.  Got my directions (hope they lead me true) and I should be on the road by 5pm.||||reg||14
